ng only if they can win with that tile. Unlikely at this stage.\n\nGiven I have only one meld, I might aim for a quick hand like All Pungs or something with honors, but I have mixed suits. Perhaps I should keep pairs of dragons and terminals. Actually, discarding W7 might be okay as it's a terminal and not part of a pair.\n\nBut let's think about potential points: I have F2 pung (no wind points), but if I get J3 pung, that's Dragon Pung (2 points). If I get another pung of terminals or honors, more points. But I need two more pungs and a pair. That's difficult.\n\nReason: I'll choose to discard a relatively safe tile that doesn't break a valuable pair. My J3 pair is valuable for Dragon Pung, so keep it. B5 and B7 pairs are possible pungs, but B5 and B7 are mid numbers, less point value. W1 pair is terminal, good for Pung of Terminals (1 point). So keep W1, B5, B7, J3 pairs. The lone tiles are W7 and B8 and F2. Among these, B8 is a terminal, but it's lone, so discard it. Also, B8 has been discarded by across twice, so likely safe.\n\nAlternatively, BuGang F2 could give me a replacement tile and I might draw something useful, but it's risky because it uses my only meld and I have to draw a tile which could be dangerous. At this early stage, I'd rather discard safely.\n\nSo I'll discard B8.\n\nAnswer: Play B8"}
